    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2m## Permission requests␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mAn agent with `--permissions ask` asks before its harness runs a tool. The␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mrequest goes through the␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mdeciders of this machine's config, `~/.config/workforce/config.toml` (or␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2m`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`), in␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mtheir order; what all of them pass on waits for you in `wf watch` and `wf␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2minbox`. Without a config,␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mthe built-in rules decide alone: a session may run its own `wf` commands.␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2m```toml␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2m[permissions]␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mguidance = "Allow reading anything and writing in the worktree. Ask about␛[0m
    ␛[2m│ ␛[0m␛[2mthe network."␛[0m
    ␛[2m│␛[0m
